  /// <summary>
  /// The VoiceChatModifierArea component can be attached to an Entity to define a region of space
  /// that changes how players speaking inside it are heard in Nearby voice chat.
  ///
  /// The Entity's Transform position determines the center-point of the region, while its size is
  /// given as a vector in the `area` property below. The Transform rotation is applied, but the scale
  /// is ignored.
  ///
  /// The effect follows the speaker: it applies to the voice of players standing inside the region,
  /// for every listener who is also standing in this scene. When a player stands inside several
  /// regions, the most restrictive value of each property wins. An excluded player is treated as
  /// outside the region, including for isolation. The region does not change PlayerVoiceState: a
  /// muted speaker is still reported as speaking.
  ///
  /// The entity cannot also carry another area component that uses a trigger region
